# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute-supervisor.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/564-headless-sdlc-execute-exits-mid-gate-when-a-stage-worker-waits-on-a-background-command/requirements.md
Feature: Headless /sdlc-execute exits mid-gate when a stage worker waits on a background command

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A headless run survives a worker waiting on a background command
    Given /sdlc-execute #N running under claude -p
    When a stage worker ends its turn behind its waiting marker while its background command runs
    Then the main loop's stop is blocked with a holding wait command
    And the session stays alive until the worker hands back and the run reaches its final result line

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: A lost session does not leave an orphaned controller
    Given a yielded headless run whose session exits before its final result
    When the supervisor sees the session heartbeat go stale
    Then the supervisor and controller end with supervising_session_lost
    And the controller lease and the merge-queue entry are released
    And a later /sdlc-execute #N resumes from branch evidence

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: A gate cut off by a lost session reruns the gate
    Given a registered gate record whose non-passing required checks are all incomplete and none failed
    When /sdlc-execute #N resumes
    Then it dispatches the gate again at the reviewed head instead of routing to implement
    And it neither reverts the prepared version nor requires a new implement commit
